<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 436)</h2>
<p><b>Loop what you mean — and mark the side you're looking at.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Repeat scope</b> joins the loop style in the transport bar: <b>This Clip</b>, <b>All Clips</b>, or a <b>Range</b> whose in/out (I/O) can cross clip boundaries — an in-point on one shot and an out three shots later plays as one repeating unit, cuts and grades intact. The range draws as a yellow band on the sequence strip, saves with the session, and follows to shared seats.</li>
<li><b>⌥L — Loop This Clip</b>: one key loops the clip under the playhead. Ping-pong and one-shot now honor whichever scope is active, and reverse playback crosses cuts too.</li>
<li><b>Paint follows the side you're working on</b> while comparing, exactly like notes: sketch on a Show B frame and the mark belongs to B — it renders, undoes, steps, and saves with B's clip, and never contaminates the other side.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
